    <item>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@djlink/117263357875250597</guid>
      <link>https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@djlink/117263357875250597</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:54:02 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Nintendo is doing well right now while XBOX and PlayStation are going through a rough patch (a 180 from 10y ago), but make no mistake, this is bad news for everyone, developers and players, no matter what system you use. The 3 ecosystems gain from the other ones being healthy.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@djlink/117263129336495504</guid>
      <link>https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@djlink/117263129336495504</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:55:55 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Reason I say this is because it seems they are treating it as main title and not a simple remake, they specifically mentioned differences from Breath of The Wild, it’s been 15 years since the last 3D Zelda with the previous structure, if they want to explore that again, having this as a gap game would be perfect for all generations of players.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@djlink/117263093261469312</guid>
      <link>https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@djlink/117263093261469312</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:46:44 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I’m super excited about Ocarina of Time Remake and not only about the game itself. I think Nintendo might be also testing the waters with younger generation of players to maybe return to traditional dungeons, less open world as their next Zelda games direction. I really hope so.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
